sentences.text:
Defecto Complainant  Petition under Section 528 of BNSS, 2023 is filed praying that in the circumstances stated in the memorandum of grounds of criminal petition,
the High Court, may be pleased to call for the records relating to and in connection with Charge Sheet vide C.C.No.1233 of 2023 on the file   Hon'ble Court of Judicial First-Class Magistrate, Pathikonda for the offence punishable under Sections 498A P./w 34 IPC and Sections 3 and 4 of D.P Act against the petitioners/Accused Nos.2 to 5 and to consequently quash the same;
Ganugapenta Venkata Lakshmi vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 7 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/72221115/
1 lA NO: 1 OF 2025:
 Petition under Section 528 of BNSS, 2023 is filed praying that in the circumstances stated in the memorandum of grounds of criminal petition,
the High Court may be pleased to grant stay of all further proceedings in C.C.No.1233 of 2023on the file of Hon'ble Court of Judicial First-Class Magistrate, Pathikonda for the offence punishable under Sections 498A R/w 34 IPC and Sections 3 and 4 of D.P Act against the petitioners/Accused No. 2 to 5 including the appearance of the petitioners herein, pending disposal of CRLP.No.11509 of 2025, on the file of the High Court.
 The petition coming on for hearing, upon perusing the Petition and memorandum of grounds of criminal petition and upon hearing the arguments of M/s Ayesha Azma.S, Advocate for the Petitioner and Public Prosecutor for the Respondent No.1, the Court rhade the following;
ORDER;
 Heard the learned counsel for the petitioners.

